demy-id "q-83725" :question/problem "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of a function $f(x)$ about $x=-1$ is given by ${P}_{2}(x)=4+3(x+1)+(x+1)^{2}.$ What is the value of ${f}^{′}(-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "This is an expansion about the point $x=-1,$ so the coefficient of the first-degree term is ${f}^{′}(-1).$ \n\nIn the given equation, we see that the coefficient of the first-degree term is $3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(-1)=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83725/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "73571ff9-24a3-52b6-be57-3ef08652ebb7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83725"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347994/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "e1b5f0d1-9d1c-533b-88eb-c719773d1ace" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347994/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "94ce07e2-30a2-5714-92e3-eb950bf12f95" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347994/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-347994/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347994" :question/id #uuid "164a6578-b0d2-53ef-82eb-e2200c88e999" :question/math-academy-id "q-347994" :question/problem "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of a function $f(x)$ about $x=2$ is given by ${P}_{2}(x)=5+3(x-2)-7(x-2)^{2}.$ What is the value of ${f}^{′}(2)?$\n\n${f}^{′}(2)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "This is an expansion about the point $x=2,$ so the coefficient of the first-degree term is ${f}^{′}(2).$ \n\nIn the given equation, we see that the coefficient of the first-degree term is $3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(2)=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-347994/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "73571ff9-24a3-52b6-be57-3ef08652ebb7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347994"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-349356/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "77e1eb4a-6a87-5512-9435-ee5a3b8565f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349356/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "18df5b77-bfb0-5f2b-9b10-c07700a19c8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349356/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad5e284d-aeab-54c1-bf71-3abfe5d3e36c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349356/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-349356/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-349356/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349356" :question/id #uuid "d5f36c02-b274-58eb-84ff-145602e4415e" :question/math-academy-id "q-349356" :question/problem "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of a function $f(x)$ about $x=-10$ is given by ${P}_{2}(x)=7-8(x+10)+15(x+10)^{2}.$ What is the value of ${f}^{″}(-10)?$\n\n${f}^{″}(-10)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "This is an expansion about the point $x=-10,$ so the coefficient of the second-degree term is $\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(-10).$ \n\nIn the given equation, we see that the coefficient of the second-degree term is $15.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(-10)=15\\,⟹\\,{f}^{″}(-10)=30.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-349356/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "73571ff9-24a3-52b6-be5