} {:db/id "q-50948" :question/id #uuid "012b69cf-240d-55ca-a054-35b0a0eb2cf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-50948" :question/problem "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of a function $f(x)$ about $x=3$ is given by ${P}_{2}(x)=1+6(x-3)+18(x-3)^{2}.$ What is the value of ${f}^{″}(3)?$" :question/worked-solution "This is an expansion about the point $x=3,$ so the coefficient of the second-degree term is $\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(3).$ \n\nIn the given equation, we see that the coefficient of the second-degree term is $18.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(3)=18\\,⟹\\,{f}^{″}(3)=36.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-50948/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "73571ff9-24a3-52b6-be57-3ef08652ebb7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50948"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-349354/field-1/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8" :answer/id #uuid "ae833cdf-b5b0-511b-8481-561f00e040aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349354/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7520d9c-3158-5c78-a3f1-909e5d62ecc0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349354/field-1/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8" :answer-field/choices ["q-349354/field-1/aa57a8d17f569b619e62bd602a6af7cff5d106888256da51f23b5b66e6987fe8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349354" :question/id #uuid "ecf46b90-08d9-5b68-ad0b-4fd74bb10bb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-349354" :question/problem "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of a function $f(x)$ about $x=9$ is given by ${P}_{2}(x)=-1+4(x-9)-13(x-9)^{2}.$ What is the value of ${f}^{″}(9)?$\n\n${f}^{″}(9)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "This is an expansion about the point $x=9,$ so the coefficient of the second-degree term is $\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(9).$ \n\nIn the given equation, we see that the coefficient of the second-degree term is $-13.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(9)=-13\\,⟹\\,{f}^{″}(9)=-26.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-349354/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "73571ff9-24a3-52b6-be57-3ef08652ebb7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-349354"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83728/selection/8905ba0a1c9ee8fb2cda1d00bc804da8f2021a379482d4dbd72afef85f8169ea" :answer/id #uuid "a454ed0c-9314-5bb3-b21d-bb2645b7412a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3+2(x-3)-(x-3)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83728/selection/771d5801fc8d40e55f1b4c2123a65e004870373887d1dbfc89b4fca6478a5b99" :answer/id #uuid "ee507a4d-15ec-5591-a4c2-935720594528" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1+2(x-3)+(x-3)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83728/selection/7a6db41160e7c9b9478fc7b858e10b43c5b1652b350ef8da0587074b18555fd9" :answer/id #uuid "f17dc244-66f4-5501-b26e-65e8dd5b9616" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2-3(x-3)-2(x-3)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83728/selection/8dd6da2856c0e84b1d59b7338270cfbe6ae09a45f784e5e9374997aa8f60cfa6" :answer/id #uuid "4be7cbeb-5cdb-58db-973f-f5931e0997d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4+3(x-3)+3(x-3)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83728/selection/92ad6a620b47d8a283d9add8e874c5f64736369674a71cab6a09b0b0417b4d7b" :answer/id #uuid "db08922e-91ad-5fa9-a011-81652c6075d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-2(x-3)+3(x-3)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83728/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a65b570c-e057-57bb-b70e-f413b516d44a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83728/selection/8905ba0a1c9ee8fb2cda1d00bc804da8f2021a379482d4dbd72afef85f8169ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-83728/selection/8905ba0a1c9ee8fb2cda1d00bc804da8f2021a379482d4dbd72afef85f8169ea" "q-83728/selection/771d5801fc8d40e55f1b4c2123a65e004870373887d1dbfc89b4fca6478a5b99" "q-83728/selection/7a6db41160e7c9b9478fc7b858e10b43c5b1652b350ef8da0587074b18555fd9" "q-83728/selection/8dd6da2856c0e84b1d59b7338270cfbe6ae09a45f784e5e9374997aa8f60cfa6" "q-83728/selection/92ad6a620b47d8a283d9add8e874c5f64736369674a71cab6a09b0b0417b4d7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83728" :question/id #uuid "a26b2381-0bbb-5cae-8272-9296c98fffe6" :question/math-academy-id "q-83728" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037233/assets/bb52a7975c917c7fe310eb29ae1daaa3438a906b84771ae5ce6998c055c4e6f7.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of a function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following could be the second-degree Taylor polynomial for $f$ about $x=3?$" :question/worked-solution "The second-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n{P}_{2}(x)=f(3)+{f}^{′}(3)(x-3)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(3)}{2}(x-3)^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the graph, we observe:\n\n- $f(3)>0.$ Therefore, the first term of the Taylor polynomial must be positive.\n\n- ${f}^{′}(3)>0,$ because the slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is positive. Therefore, the coefficient of the second term in the Taylor polynomial must be positive.\n\n- ${f}^{″}(3)<0,$ because the graph is concave down at $x=3.$ Therefore, the coefficient of the third term in the Taylor polynomial must be negative.\n\nThe only option that meets the above criteria is\n\n$$\n{P}_{2}(x)=3+2(x-3)-(x-3)^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83728/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fce4cd5a-537a-5eb4-a610-59d2bad95a89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83728"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-81063"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037233/assets/e483403ebe85920111334dacfc22dc907ab3c33cd38b33361d7634132032c811.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of a function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following could be the second-degree Taylor polynomial for $f$ about $x=1?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-83729/selection/a1ecb694638718ea5888869c2e6e0c966b04e65a387d0173aeeae70ab4855f2e" :answer/id #uuid "c956c25c-c09d-5540-a6df-0bb1ad7324fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3+3(x+2)+(x+2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83729/selection/7eaf4c087ec3da0d8e6edab4beb6d2878d148b5c6d278fc4f0bf10a3666cf497" :answer/id #uuid "c74d2c8d-6072-5314-ad5e-2c422f561d32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4-2(x+2)-(x+2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83729/selection/e9f67333b30c7ea240c3e430aedba951651754b719864996dfdbc3a09ca9f804" :answer/id #uuid "3d99aa3b-a82c-5dd7-91df-1f8843ceafdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+(x+2)+2(x+2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83729/selection/2e905edd760af1c6dc4585a3b6dd37db02c116c204b4f56207e52e9229a2528f" :answer/id #uuid "762edd02-fbb7-5f82-9f8d-9c4d0784e560" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3(x+2)-2(x+2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83729/selection/1f9b48e49eb3f1d79b18213ff2edf7bd991c95fd5ef77512cf481ba47fe65529" :answer/id #uuid "bcfc9eff-a9f5-53da-97fd-bbb458330119" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3+2(x+2)-(x+2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83729/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "252a0d36-fd03-5b8f-8aa3-ad6ac91ea3b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83729/selection/1f9b48e49eb3f1d79b18213ff2edf7bd991c95fd5ef77512cf481ba47fe65529" :answer-field/choices ["q-83729/selection/a1ecb694638718ea5888869c2e6e0c966b04e65a387d0173aeeae70ab4855f2e" "q-83729/selection/7eaf4c087ec3da0d8e6edab4beb6d2878d148b5c6d278fc4f0bf10a3666cf497" "q-83729/selection/e9f67333b30c7ea240c3e430aedba951651754b719864996dfdbc3a09ca9f804" "q-83729/selection/2e905edd760af1c6dc4585a3b6dd37db02c116c204b4f56207e52e9229a2528f" "q-83729/selection/1f9b48e49eb3f1d79b18213ff2edf7bd991c95fd5ef77512cf481ba47fe65529"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83729" :question/id #uuid "fd80e409-455c-5dd2-b392-fb0349ca3a48" :question/math-academy-id "q-83729" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037233/assets/9fe49372324dac217bb8e96ae6f485fe74308184ec9dd197fc98b973560dd8af.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of a function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following could be the second-degree Taylor polynomial for $f$ about $x=-2?$" :question/worked-solution "The second-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x=-2$ is \n\n$$\n{P}_{2}(x)=f(-2)+{f}^{′}(-2)(x+2)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(-2)}{2}(x+2)^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the graph, we observe:\n\n- $f(-2)>0.$ Therefore, the first term of the Taylor polynomial must be positive.\n\n- ${f}^{′}(-2)>0,$ because the slope of the tangent at $x=-2$ is positive. Therefore, the coefficient of the second term in the Taylor polynomial must be positive.\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-2)<0,$ because the graph is concave down at $x=-2.$ Therefore, the coefficient of the third term in the Taylor polynomial must be negative.\n\nThe only option that meets the above criteria is\n\n$$\n{P}_{2}(x)=3+2(x+2)-(x+2)^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83729/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fce4cd5a-537a-5eb4-a610-59d2bad95a89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83729"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125822/selection/8296a4778a634ac91ebc4ce79027c02607363c18c8051212817b1e779349b94a" :answer/id #uuid "dc521d82-5e02-5e2b-b19b-9cd83c08a412" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1+3(x+2)-5(x+2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125822/selection/afa8527034df4073f9465d9fd463d967a74151f43326152431db